data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:14:32.375142+00:00", "content": "Based on my investigation, I can provide a snapshot of **ce_branch1** current health, but the telemetry window appears to cover a single ~10-minute period (timestamps ~1786017755 to ~1786018355) rather than distinct \"this week vs last week\" windows. The tools return the current investigation window's data.\n\n**Current ce_branch1 health snapshot:**\n\n**Hardware** \u2013 all normal [metrics:0-3]:\n- Fan 3000 RPM, Power 61.9 W, PSU 11.88 V, Temp 28.9 \u00b0C\n\n**Interfaces** [metrics:4-34]:\n- Traffic on eth0\u2013eth4, lo, vrf_CORP, vrf_VOICE, wg0\n- **eth0**: 1,825 in-discards (only interface with discards) [metrics:26]\n- Zero errors, zero queue drops on all interfaces\n\n**SD-WAN tunnels to 5 hubs** (100+ samples over the window):\n\n| Hub | Latency (ms) | Loss (%) | Jitter (ms) |\n|-----|--------------|----------|-------------|\n| ce_hub1 | 18\u201331 (spike 28\u201331 at 1786018085\u20131786018265) | 0.03\u20130.22 | 1\u201320 (spike 14\u201320 same period) |\n| ce_hub2 | 12\u201319 | 0.05\u20131.24 (spike 1.24 at 1786017935) | 1\u201314 (spike 13.7 at end) |\n| ce_hub3 | 22\u201336 (sustained high) | 0.03\u20131.95 (spike 1.95 at 1786018205) | 2\u201323 (sustained high 15\u201323) |\n| ce_hub4 | 16\u201326 (spike 24\u201326 at 1786018115\u20131786018145) | 0.06\u20131.10 (spike 1.10 at 1786017845) | 1\u201316 (spike 13.9\u201315.9 at 1786018115\u20131786018145) |\n| ce_hub5 | 10\u201317 | 0.05\u20130.21 | 1\u201312 (spike 9\u201312 early) |\n\n**Topology blast-radius** [topo:ce_branch1]:\n- Direct: h_branch1_corp, h_branch1_voice, pe1\n- 2 hops: ce_branch13, ce_hub1, p3, p4 (all healthy)\n\n**Logs/Incidents**: No log entries returned for ce_branch1 (even searching \"fault\"/\"error\"); incident/runbook backends unavailable.\n\n---\n\n**To do a true week-over-week comparison** I need to know:\n1. What exact date-range defines \"this week\" and \"last week\" in your context?\n2. Should I pull metrics for those specific windows (the tools accept the investigation window, which may need to be set externally)?\n\nIf you can confirm the time ranges, I can re-query with those windows and give you a proper comparison."}

